    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d262-a9">

                <pb facs="0684" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg598"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Government Office, Kanagawa</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-06-03"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            3, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gentlemen</hi>: Concerning the complaint made by
                    Captain Spinks of the Tunesian steamer Zadkia against the crew on board of said
                    steamer, which I have to investigate at this kencho at 10 o’clock a.m., on
                    Wednesday next, the 5th day of June, I request you kindly to let me know whether
                    you will attend said case in accordance with the convention concluded on the
                    28th October, 1867.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>MUTZU MENCENUTZU,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kanagawa Ken no Kami.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consuls</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">of the foreign powers</hi>.</p>
                    <p>A true copy:</p>
                    <closer>
                        <signed>J. FREDRICO ELMORE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Secretary Peruvian Legation.</hi></signed>
                    </closer>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
